# Auto-Update System

## Architecture

```
┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│                   React (renderer)                   │
│                                                      │
│  useAppUpdate() → { status, version, check, install }│
│       │                                              │
│       ├── Electron? → IPC → main process             │
│       │                      autoUpdater             │
│       │                      (electron-updater)      │
│       │                                              │
│       └── PWA? → ServiceWorker                       │
│                  reg.waiting.postMessage(SKIP_WAITING)│
└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
```

## React — unified hook

```tsx
import { useAppUpdate } from "~/shared/lib/updater";

function UpdateBanner() {
  const { status, version, percent, check, install } = useAppUpdate();

  if (status === "ready") {
    return (
      <div>
        Version {version} is available
        <button onClick={install}>Update</button>
      </div>
    );
  }

  if (status === "downloading") {
    return <div>Downloading update... {percent}%</div>;
  }

  return null;
}
```

## Statuses

| Status | Electron | PWA |
|--------|----------|-----|
| `idle` | Waiting | Waiting |
| `checking` | autoUpdater.checkForUpdates() | reg.update() |
| `available` | New version detected | — |
| `downloading` | Downloading in background | installing SW |
| `ready` | Downloaded, awaiting restart | SW waiting |
| `up-to-date` | Current version is up to date | — |
| `error` | Download/check error | — |

## Electron

- Check on startup + every hour
- `autoDownload: true` — download in background
- `autoInstallOnAppQuit: true` — install on close
- User can expedite: `install()` → `quitAndInstall()`
- Download progress via `download-progress` event

### electron-builder.yml

```yaml
publish:
  provider: generic
  url: https://update.workspace.example.com/releases
```

The update server serves `latest.yml` / `latest-mac.yml` / `latest-linux.yml` + binaries.

## PWA

- On every visit the browser checks the SW
- If a new SW is found → `updatefound` → `installing` → `installed`
- When the new SW is ready → `status: "ready"`
- `install()` → `postMessage({ type: "SKIP_WAITING" })` → page reload

## For AI Agent

- When adding an update button — use the `useAppUpdate()` hook
- Do not call `autoUpdater` or `serviceWorker` directly from components
- Update status is read-only in components; actions are via `check()` and `install()`
